{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/server/app-config.ts | sed -n '440,590p'; git diff settings-ui-integration...HEAD -- Dockerfile compose.yml .env.example README.md | sed -n '1,400p'; rg -n \\\"VITE_(CHILD|APP|STORY)|build:\\\\s*\"'$|args:\" compose.yml README.md .env.example Dockerfile'","aggregated_output":"   440\t\n   441\t/**\n   442\t * Forme envoyée au parent — construite PURE depuis (lignes, fallback) pour le\n   443\t * golden « boundary secret-scan » : aucun champ ne porte jamais un secret,\n   444\t * seulement {configured, hint}.\n   445\t */\n   446\texport function settingsStatusFromRows(\n   447\t  rows: Rows,\n   448\t  fallback: AppConfig\n   449\t): AppSettingsStatus {\n   450\t  const config = configFromRows(rows, fallback);\n   451\t  return {\n   452\t    branding: {\n   453\t      appDescription: valueStatus(\n   454\t        rows,\n   455\t        \"branding:app-description\",\n   456\t        config.branding.appDescription\n   457\t      ),\n   458\t      appName: valueStatus(rows, \"branding:app-name\", config.branding.appName),\n   459\t      childName: valueStatus(\n   460\t        rows,\n   461\t        \"branding:child-name\",\n   462\t        config.branding.childName\n   463\t      ),\n   464\t      storyLabel: valueStatus(\n   465\t        rows,\n   466\t        \"branding:story-label\",\n   467\t        config.branding.storyLabel\n   468\t      ),\n   469\t    },\n   470\t    features: featureStatuses(config.provider),\n   471\t    provider: {\n   472\t      anthropicApiKey: secretStatus(\n   473\t        rows,\n   474\t        \"text:anthropic-api-key\",\n   475\t        config.provider.anthropicApiKey\n   476\t      ),\n   477\t      defaultLang: valueStatus(\n   478\t        rows,\n   479\t        \"story:default-lang\",\n   480\t        config.provider.defaultLang\n   481\t      ),\n   482\t      elevenLabsApiKey: secretStatus(\n   483\t        rows,\n   484\t        \"tts:elevenlabs-api-key\",\n   485\t        config.provider.elevenLabsApiKey\n   486\t      ),\n   487\t      geminiApiKey: secretStatus(\n   488\t        rows,\n   489\t        \"image:gemini-api-key\",\n   490\t        config.provider.geminiApiKey\n   491\t      ),\n   492\t      imageEnabled: valueStatus(\n   493\t        rows,\n   494\t        \"image:enabled\",\n   495\t        config.provider.imageEnabled\n   496\t      ),\n   497\t      imageModel: valueStatus(rows, \"image:model\", config.provider.imageModel),\n   498\t      imageResolution: valueStatus(\n   499\t        rows,\n   500\t        \"image:resolution\",\n   501\t        config.provider.imageResolution\n   502\t      ),\n   503\t      storyModel: valueStatus(\n   504\t        rows,\n   505\t        \"text:story-model\",\n   506\t        config.provider.storyModel\n   507\t      ),\n   508\t      ttsEnabled: valueStatus(rows, \"tts:enabled\", config.provider.ttsEnabled),\n   509\t      ttsProvider: valueStatus(\n   510\t        rows,\n   511\t        \"tts:provider\",\n   512\t        config.provider.ttsProvider\n   513\t      ),\n   514\t    },\n   515\t  };\n   516\t}\n   517\t\n   518\t// ── Écritures centrales (validation + normalisation UNIQUEMENT ici) ─────────\n   519\t\n   520\texport type SettingPatchOp =\n   521\t  | { key: string; op: \"set\"; value: string }\n   522\t  | { key: string; op: \"delete\" };\n   523\t\n   524\t/** Même idiome maison que les *-functions.ts (espace, 23 caractères). */\n   525\tfunction nowSqlTimestamp(): string {\n   526\t  return new Date().toISOString().replace(\"T\", \" \").slice(0, 23);\n   527\t}\n   528\t\n   529\tfunction assertWritableKey(key: string): void {\n   530\t  if (!WRITABLE_KEYS.includes(key)) {\n   531\t    throw new Error(`Clé de réglage inconnue: ${key}`);\n   532\t  }\n   533\t}\n   534\t\n   535\t/**\n   536\t * Applique un PATCH au niveau champ dans UNE transaction (db.batch libSQL,\n   537\t * atomique) : deux onglets qui sauvent des sections disjointes ne s'écrasent\n   538\t * jamais ; un batch qui échoue ne change rien. TOUT écrivain passe ici (y\n   539\t * compris saveUiLocaleFn) — la validation de clé ne peut pas être contournée.\n   540\t */\n   541\texport async function applySettingsPatch(\n   542\t  operations: readonly SettingPatchOp[]\n   543\t): Promise<void> {\n   544\t  for (const operation of operations) {\n   545\t    assertWritableKey(operation.key);\n   546\t  }\n   547\t  if (operations.length === 0) {\n   548\t    return;\n   549\t  }\n   550\t  const { db } = await import(\"~/server/db\");\n   551\t  const statements = operations.map((operation) =>\n   552\t    operation.op === \"set\"\n   553\t      ? db\n   554\t          .insert(appSettings)\n   555\t          .values({ key: operation.key, value: operation.value })\n   556\t          .onConflictDoUpdate({\n   557\t            set: { updatedAt: nowSqlTimestamp(), value: operation.value },\n   558\t            target: appSettings.key,\n   559\t          })\n   560\t      : db.delete(appSettings).where(eq(appSettings.key, operation.key))\n   561\t  );\n   562\t  const [first, ...rest] = statements;\n   563\t  if (!first) {\n   564\t    return;\n   565\t  }\n   566\t  await db.batch([first, ...rest]);\n   567\t}\n   568\t\n   569\t/** Pose une valeur (upsert). Passe par applySettingsPatch — une transaction. */\n   570\texport function setSetting(key: string, value: string): Promise<void> {\n   571\t  return applySettingsPatch([{ key, op: \"set\", value }]);\n   572\t}\n   573\t\n   574\t/** Supprime la ligne — « revenir au réglage du déploiement » (l'env reprend). */\n   575\texport function deleteSetting(key: string): Promise<void> {\n   576\t  return applySettingsPatch([{ key, op: \"delete\" }]);\n   577\t}\ndiff --git a/.env.example b/.env.example\nindex c03885b..937dc9b 100644\n--- a/.env.example\n+++ b/.env.example\n@@ -1,47 +1,46 @@\n-# ─── Text (required) ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n-# The Anthropic key is what writes the stories.\n-ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=\n-# Model used to write the stories (fine as-is).\n-STORY_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8\n+# ─── Almost everything is set IN THE APP now ──────────────────────\n+# Keys, models, images, voice and branding live in the database and are\n+# managed at /parents/reglages (Settings). Values below act as the\n+# DEPLOYMENT DEFAULTS: they apply only when nothing is set in the UI\n+# (\"réglage du déploiement\" badge). A fresh install can leave this file\n+# empty, boot, and paste the Anthropic key in the UI.\n \n-# ─── Database — local SQLite file (optional) ──────────────────────\n-# Defaults to file:<DATA_DIR>/app.db (in Docker: the app-data volume).\n-# Migrations apply automatically at startup. Only set this to move the file;\n-# it must stay a file: URL.\n+# ─── Infra (env only — cannot live in the database) ───────────────\n+# Local SQLite file. Defaults to file:<DATA_DIR>/app.db (in Docker: the\n+# app-data volume). Migrations apply automatically at startup. Only set\n+# this to move the file; it must stay a file: URL.\n # DATABASE_URL=file:./data/app.db\n+# Disk folder for generated images/audio + the SQLite db (in Docker this is\n+# the app-data volume). On an ephemeral filesystem (no volume), set\n+# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN instead (Vercel Blob) — media only; the db file\n+# still needs a persistent disk.\n+DATA_DIR=./data\n+# Extra hostnames the Vite DEV server accepts (Vite blocks unknown Host\n+# headers). Only needed when reaching `bun run dev` through a reverse proxy\n+# or tunnel; comma-separated. Keep real domains in the gitignored .env.\n+DEV_ALLOWED_HOSTS=\n \n-# ─── Images (optional) — disabled by default ──────────────────────\n-# Set IMAGE_ENABLED=true and fill GEMINI_API_KEY for illustrations.\n+# ─── Deployment defaults (optional — the UI wins) ─────────────────\n+# Text: the Anthropic key writes the stories; model fine as-is.\n+ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=\n+STORY_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8\n+# Images (off by default): IMAGE_ENABLED=true + GEMINI_API_KEY.\n IMAGE_ENABLED=false\n GEMINI_API_KEY=\n IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-image\n-\n-# ─── Voice (optional) — disabled by default ───────────────────────\n-# Set TTS_ENABLED=true for the \"Listen\" button.\n-# TTS_PROVIDER=edge (free, French voices) or elevenlabs (premium).\n+# Voice (off by default): TTS_ENABLED=true shows the \"Listen\" button.\n+# TTS_PROVIDER=edge (free) or elevenlabs (premium, needs its key).\n TTS_ENABLED=false\n TTS_PROVIDER=edge\n ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=\n+DEFAULT_LANG=fr\n \n-# ─── Branding (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────\n-# Personalize without touching the code (defaults in src/config/app.ts).\n-# VITE_CHILD_NAME=Léa derives everything: app name \"L'atelier de Léa\"\n-# (browser tab + home header) and booklet footer \"Une histoire de Léa\"\n+# ─── Branding (legacy deployment defaults — prefer the UI) ────────\n+# Set the child's name and workshop texts at /parents/reglages instead.\n+# These remain honored as fallbacks for existing deployments:\n+# VITE_CHILD_NAME=Léa derives \"L'atelier de Léa\" + \"Une histoire de Léa\"\n # (\"de\" elides to \"d'\" before a vowel: Arsène → \"d'Arsène\").\n VITE_CHILD_NAME=\n-# Full-string overrides, when the derived phrasing doesn't fit:\n VITE_APP_NAME=\n VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION=\n VITE_STORY_LABEL=\n-\n-# ─── Misc ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n-DEFAULT_LANG=fr\n-# Disk folder for generated images/audio + the SQLite db (in Docker this is\n-# the app-data volume). On an ephemeral filesystem (no volume), set\n-# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN instead (Vercel Blob) — media only; the db file\n-# still needs a persistent disk.\n-DATA_DIR=./data\n-# Extra hostnames the Vite DEV server accepts (Vite blocks unknown Host\n-# headers). Only needed when reaching `bun run dev` through a reverse proxy\n-# or tunnel; comma-separated. Keep real domains in the gitignored .env.\n-DEV_ALLOWED_HOSTS=\ndiff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile\nindex 7ef9094..37e1e90 100644\n--- a/Dockerfile\n+++ b/Dockerfile\n@@ -8,7 +8,10 @@ WORKDIR /app\n COPY package.json bun.lock ./\n RUN bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts\n COPY . .\n-# VITE_* vars are compile-time (baked into the client bundle) → build args.\n+# LEGACY-OPTIONNEL (env→DB, v0.6) : la marque se règle désormais à\n+# /parents/reglages (table app_settings) ; ces args ne servent plus que de\n+# SECOURS pour un déploiement existant qui n'a rien posé en base. Gardés une\n+# release, suppression envisagée ensuite (TODOS.md).\n ARG VITE_CHILD_NAME\n ARG VITE_APP_NAME\n ARG VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION\n@@ -19,6 +22,16 @@ RUN SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION=1 bun run build\n FROM node:22-slim\n WORKDIR /app\n ENV NODE_ENV=production PORT=3009\n+# Secours legacy runtime (mêmes valeurs que les build args) : le serveur lit\n+# process.env.VITE_* quand aucune ligne branding:* n'existe en base.\n+ARG VITE_CHILD_NAME\n+ARG VITE_APP_NAME\n+ARG VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION\n+ARG VITE_STORY_LABEL\n+ENV VITE_CHILD_NAME=$VITE_CHILD_NAME \\\n+    VITE_APP_NAME=$VITE_APP_NAME \\\n+    VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION=$VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION \\\n+    VITE_STORY_LABEL=$VITE_STORY_LABEL\n COPY --from=build /app/.output ./.output\n # Migrations auto-apply at startup (src/server/db/index.ts) and are resolved\n # from the CWD — ship the folder next to the server bundle.\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 65b71dc..bf0fe2c 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -62,13 +62,15 @@ moment.\n \n Two files to personalize (plus in-app management at `/parents`):\n \n-- `src/config/app.ts` — the app's display name and booklet footer. Prefer\n-  setting `VITE_CHILD_NAME=Léa` (see `.env.example`) to derive both without\n-  touching the code; `VITE_APP_NAME` / `VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION` /\n-  `VITE_STORY_LABEL` override the full strings. `VITE_CHILD_NAME` also names\n-  the desktop's user: the session-screen portrait is the hero whose name\n-  matches it (case-, accent- and d'-elision-tolerant) — no match, or no\n-  configured name, falls back to a soft star and the app name.\n+- **The child's name and workshop texts** — set them in the app at\n+  `/parents/reglages` (\"Le prénom & l'atelier\"): the browser tab, the\n+  session-screen portrait and the printed booklet footer follow on the next\n+  reload, no rebuild. The name also names the desktop's user: the portrait\n+  is the hero whose name matches it (case-, accent- and\n+  d'-elision-tolerant) — no match, or no configured name, falls back to a\n+  soft star and the workshop name. The legacy `VITE_CHILD_NAME` /\n+  `VITE_APP_NAME` / `VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION` / `VITE_STORY_LABEL` env vars\n+  remain honored as deployment defaults when nothing is set in the UI.\n - `src/config/characters.ts` — the heroes: replace the sample kids with your\n   child, siblings, friends. The default hero is pre-selected in the wizard.\n   Places, surprise elements and doudous have the same kind of config files\n@@ -80,16 +82,18 @@ Requirements: [Bun](https://bun.sh) and an [Anthropic API\n key](https://console.anthropic.com/). The database is a local SQLite file\n (created automatically under `data/` on first start — nothing to set up).\n \n-### 1. Fill `.env.local`\n+### 1. Get your Anthropic key ready\n \n-Copy `.env.example` to `.env.local` and paste the value:\n+The app boots with **zero configuration**. After the first start, open\n+**http://localhost:3009/parents/reglages** and paste your Anthropic key in\n+the \"Les histoires\" card — it applies to the next story immediately.\n \n-```\n-ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-key\n-```\n+(Alternative: copy `.env.example` to `.env.local` and set\n+`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=` there as a deployment default — anything set in the UI\n+wins over it.)\n \n Images and voice are **disabled** by default — the app works great text-only\n-(only the value above is required).\n+(only the Anthropic key is needed).\n \n ### 2. Install\n \n@@ -112,13 +116,21 @@ bun run build\n bun run start\n ```\n \n-## Settings (`.env.local`)\n+## Settings\n \n-| Setting | What it does |\n+**Keys, models, images, voice and branding are managed in the app** at\n+`/parents/reglages`. Settings live in the database (`app_settings`), apply\n+to the next operation (no restart, no rebuild), and each field shows a\n+\"réglage du déploiement\" badge while the env default applies. Secret keys\n+never travel back to the browser — the page only shows a masked hint.\n+\n+Environment variables act as **deployment defaults** (a UI value always\n+wins; \"Revenir au réglage du déploiement\" deletes the UI value and the env\n+default resumes):\n+\n+| Env default | What it does |\n | --- | --- |\n-| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | **Required.** The key that writes the stories. |\n-| `DATABASE_URL` | Optional. Moves the SQLite file (`file:` URL only; defaults to `file:<DATA_DIR>/app.db`). |\n-| `DATA_DIR` | Optional. Where the SQLite db and generated media live (default `./data`; in Docker, the `app-data` volume). |\n+| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | The key that writes the stories (or paste it in the UI). |\n | `STORY_MODEL` | The model used (fine as-is). |\n | `IMAGE_ENABLED` | `true` to add illustrations (otherwise a soft color block). |\n | `GEMINI_API_KEY` | The Google key, needed IF images are enabled. |\n@@ -126,21 +138,29 @@ bun run start\n | `TTS_PROVIDER` | `edge` (free, French voices) or `elevenlabs` (premium). |\n | `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` | The key, needed IF you pick `elevenlabs`. |\n \n-Restart `bun run dev` after changing a setting.\n+True infra stays env-only (restart to change):\n+\n+| Setting | What it does |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| `DATABASE_URL` | Optional. Moves the SQLite file (`file:` URL only; defaults to `file:<DATA_DIR>/app.db`). |\n+| `DATA_DIR` | Optional. Where the SQLite db and generated media live (default `./data`; in Docker, the `app-data` volume). |\n+\n+**Backup note:** since keys can live in the database, `app.db` (and the\n+`app-data` volume) now deserves the same care as `.env` files.\n \n ## Deploying (Docker)\n \n The repo ships a `Dockerfile` (multi-stage: Bun build → `node:22-slim`\n runtime) and a `compose.yml`. On the deploy machine:\n \n-1. Create `.env.production` at the repo root with the runtime settings\n-   (same names as the table above: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, plus any optional\n-   image/TTS settings).\n-2. The `VITE_*` branding vars are baked in at **build time**. `compose.yml`\n-   forwards `VITE_CHILD_NAME` from a root `.env` file (Docker Compose reads\n-   it for `${...}` substitution); the three full-string overrides\n-   (`VITE_APP_NAME`, `VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION`, `VITE_STORY_LABEL`) currently\n-   need a `compose.override.yml` or explicit build args.\n+1. Create `.env.production` at the repo root — it can be minimal (even\n+   empty): keys and options are set in the UI at `/parents/reglages` after\n+   the first boot. Any value you do set there acts as the deployment\n+   default (same names as the tables above).\n+2. (Legacy, optional) The `VITE_*` branding vars remain honored as\n+   deployment defaults — prefer the \"Le prénom & l'atelier\" card in the UI.\n+   `compose.yml` still forwards `VITE_CHILD_NAME` from a root `.env` file\n+   for existing deployments.\n 3. Then:\n \n ```\nDockerfile:15:ARG VITE_CHILD_NAME\nDockerfile:16:ARG VITE_APP_NAME\nDockerfile:17:ARG VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION\nDockerfile:18:ARG VITE_STORY_LABEL\nDockerfile:27:ARG VITE_CHILD_NAME\nDockerfile:28:ARG VITE_APP_NAME\nDockerfile:29:ARG VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION\nDockerfile:30:ARG VITE_STORY_LABEL\nDockerfile:31:ENV VITE_CHILD_NAME=$VITE_CHILD_NAME \\\nDockerfile:32:    VITE_APP_NAME=$VITE_APP_NAME \\\nDockerfile:33:    VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION=$VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION \\\nDockerfile:34:    VITE_STORY_LABEL=$VITE_STORY_LABEL\n.env.example:41:# VITE_CHILD_NAME=Léa derives \"L'atelier de Léa\" + \"Une histoire de Léa\"\n.env.example:43:VITE_CHILD_NAME=\n.env.example:44:VITE_APP_NAME=\n.env.example:45:VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION=\n.env.example:46:VITE_STORY_LABEL=\ncompose.yml:8:    build:\ncompose.yml:10:      args:\ncompose.yml:11:        VITE_CHILD_NAME: ${VITE_CHILD_NAME:-}\nREADME.md:71:  soft star and the workshop name. The legacy `VITE_CHILD_NAME` /\nREADME.md:72:  `VITE_APP_NAME` / `VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION` / `VITE_STORY_LABEL` env vars\nREADME.md:162:   `compose.yml` still forwards `VITE_CHILD_NAME` from a root `.env` file\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
